<XPD:BODY><XPD:OBJ name="DocumentElement" type="UMLProject" guid="oOxEPYtTRDi8vqFbgR4kbgAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Title" type="string">Stock Management System - Use Case Model</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedElements" type="integer">1</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedElements[0]" type="UMLModel" guid="lWDFH9N8QJ+IkkeH9St3cAAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Name" type="string">Use Case Model</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="StereotypeProfile" type="string">UMLStandard</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="StereotypeName" type="string">useCaseModel</XPD:ATTR><XPD:REF name="Namespace">oOxEPYtTRDi8vqFbgR4kbgAA</XPD:REF><XPD:ATTR name="Documentation" type="string">Source: sms.md class definitions, operations, relationship matrix and ambiguity notes. This is a use case interpretation of that design, not a newly supplied full SRS. Role assignments follow the explicitly identified inferences in sms.md: Store Staff maintain items/record movements, Warehouse Manager transfers/adjusts stock, Procurement Staff reorders. Reporting permissions are unspecified; report access for the three human roles is an editable assumption. Reorder checks use the configured per-location or total-stock scope; the source leaves this open. A low-stock alert does not automatically create a purchase order. Hardware, internal entities, enumerations and audit records are not actors. Authentication/authorization are preconditions for restricted operations.</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedDiagrams" type="integer">1</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedDiagrams[0]" type="UMLUseCaseDiagram" guid="UcjONd77ScWFopHDc2PepAAA"><XPD:ATTR name="Name" type="string">Stock Management System - Use Cases</XPD:ATTR><XPD:ATTR name="DefaultDiagram" type="boolean">True</XPD:ATTR><XPD:REF name="DiagramOwner">lWDFH9N8QJ+IkkeH9St3cAAA</XPD:REF><XPD:OBJ name="DiagramView" type="UMLUseCaseDiagramView" guid="lX+VzZAKT6mNLsIAFMR1BAAA"><XPD:REF name="Diagram">UcjONd77ScWFopHDc2PepAAA</XPD:REF><XPD:ATTR name="#OwnedViews" type="integer">41</XPD:ATTR><XPD:OBJ name="OwnedViews[0]